The app's purpose is to allow small businesses to upload information about their restaurant and menu. Other user's will then be able to order menu items such as food from these restaurants. Furthermore, the businesses can set a donation goal for their restaurant. This will be visible to other user's and will serve as a way to help smaller restaurants to gain funding through peopple who are interested in their restaurant and will likely be potential customers if they are already donating to the funding of that restaurant and their business.

The techology stack that I am using is the MERN stack. I am using mongo db for storing the data such as the restaurant's and the user's data.  Next, I am using express for the backend. I am using React for my frontend since I want to learn how to use it in a project for future use. Finally, I am using node.

The UI/UX considerations include many things such as the best way to display the restaurant's information to the user to make it easy for users to understand what the restaurant is, what it provides and what it is asking of the user. Secondly, I have considered the way that users will interact with each function of the website and how that may differ from the intended result. Finally, I have considered the user's journey and how easy it is for them to follow along.

The first main feature my web app has is the ablity for businesses to add a restaurant by entering its name, goal for donations, and its menu. Secondly, the ability for user's to see all available restaurants and be able to donate to them. Eventually, another feature will allow user's to add mnu items to their basket. The final feature that I wish to add is for businesses to view theirrestaurant's stats and sales information.

The challenges that I still anticipate first include displaying the content in a way that is easy to understand but a way that is also pleasant to look at. Secondly, storing the data such as the images for the restaurants in an efficient way so that the web app doesn't break when potentially scaled further.

The first experiment I did was trying to input the restaurant names and having them display in Mongo DB. The second experiment was trying to do the same with images which was a lot harder due to the way images have to be stored and recieved. Thirdly, I experimented with user and business accountsd to display different information based on the type of account. Finally, I am currently experimenting with adding menu items manually through business accounts and displaying or purchasing them on the suer side.

I have learnt how express works properly with the backend, including get and post requests and how much you can actualluy do with that. Secondly, I have learnt how to create and manipulate my own collection of data in order to create a satosfying user experience. Finally, I have learnt how to manage user accounts.
